    isbefore: []  # 8bd9
    duplicate_of: []  # 8bd9
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 8bd9
    pr_ref:  # 8bd9
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family L). Stand-alone finding F26.6 previously folded onto INV-luhur. Full evidence on INV-luhur's pass-26 discussion entry.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`profile.languages.<lang>.loc` 1.66× double-counts vs `Σ(node.lines_of_code)`:\n\n- python: profile=481203 vs Σ=801588 (Σ exceeds profile; nested-symbol double-count)\n- file-kind LOC = 0\n- non-symbol analyzers Σ = 0\n\nThe discrepancy: `profile.compute_profile` reads LOC per-file once; `node.lines_of_code` is populated on every method/class/function — nested symbols inflate the sum.\n\n## Invariant\n\nEither:\n1. **`Σ(node.lines_of_code) == file's actual LOC`** — only file-kind nodes carry LOC; method/class/function nodes have LOC=None. Eliminates double-count by construction.\n2. **`Σ(node.lines_of_code where kind=='file')` is the canonical sum**, documented in spec.md; nested symbols carry their own LOC for span-aware queries.\n\nPath (2) preserves the per-symbol LOC signal for span-aware tooling. Path (1) is simpler but loses per-symbol granularity.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nDocument the derivation rule. Add a `metrics.loc_methodology` field describing the aggregation rule. If choosing path (2), consumer tooling adjusts to filter on kind before summing.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F26.6** — INV-luhur discussion entry 2026-06-03 (pass-26 batch).\n\nLab notebook: pass 26.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-luhur**.\n- Sibling: **WI-metrics-languages-files-empty** (Family F — adjacent profile/metrics discrepancy).\n- Family L siblings."  # 8bd9
    fields: {}  # 8bd9
- op: discuss  # c343
  at: '2026-06-06T10:36:49Z'  # c343
  by: agent  # c343
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c343
  clock: 2  # c343
  nonce: c343  # c343
  message: "CORRECTION: the inflation SUBJECT is reversed, the ratio does not generalize, and 9 languages emit no per-symbol LOC (blind-severity-derived priority signal: P2). This item says profile.languages.<lang>.loc 1.66x double-counts vs Σ(node.lines_of_code). The actual direction is reversed: for Python, Σ(node.loc)=806116 vs profile.loc=483677, so the node-sum is ≈1.667x the profile — the per-symbol node sum is the INFLATED side (nested class/method spans overlap and double-count), while profile.loc is the smaller, correct file-level SLOC. The ~1.66x magnitude holds only for Python; the profile/node ratio swings across languages (bash 2.10, go 1.27, rust 1.44 with profile larger; python 0.60, typescript 0.43, javascript 0.90 with node-sum larger). And 9 languages have profile.loc>0 but per-symbol node-LOC sum=0 (html, json, markdown, yaml, toml, sql, wgsl, solidity, xml). Fix the recorded framing + the per-language node-LOC summation."  # c343
